{"review_id":"00001788306112275771-0004098830-000002-cycle-review-1","reviewed_manifest_hash":"sha256:fc3f9245dba27bca0abff594f05784fb75a9424a1ceca747361f718e6916a3ab","findings":[{"finding_id":"F1-body-read-error-misclassified","category":"correctness_defect","severity":"high","blocking":false,"title":"Response-body read failure is classified Retryable, not Ambiguous, after the provider has already accepted the request","claim":"`OpenAiResponsesClient::submit` routes the error from `response.text().await` through `map_transport_error`, which classifies every non-timeout `reqwest::Error` as `Retryable(TransientTransport)` on the stated grounds that \"the request never reached the provider ... so nothing was billed\". That reasoning does not hold at this call site: status and headers have already been received, so the provider has accepted, executed and billed the request; a failure while reading the body is exactly the mid-stream cutoff the module elsewhere insists must be `Ambiguous`. The result is a billable attempt reported as a free retry with no usage recorded, contradicting both the acceptance criterion on ambiguous completion and this change's own contract text.","evidence":[{"kind":"diff_hunk","path":"crates/familiar-ai-llm/src/openai_api.rs","hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,1367 @@\n+        let status = response.status();\n+        let retry_after_ms = response\n+            .headers()\n+            .get(reqwest::header::RETRY_AFTER)\n+            .and_then(|value| value.to_str().ok())\n+            .and_then(|value| value.parse::<u64>().ok())\n+            .map(|seconds| seconds * 1000);\n+        let text = response.text().await.map_err(map_transport_error)?;"},{"kind":"diff_hunk","path":"crates/familiar-ai-llm/src/openai_api.rs","hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,1367 @@\n+fn map_transport_error(error: reqwest::Error) -> AdapterError {\n+    if error.is_timeout() {\n+        // The request may have already reached the provider and been\n+        // billed; a client-side timeout waiting for a response is the\n+        // honest ambiguous case, never a free retry.\n+        AdapterError::Ambiguous {\n+            reason: \"OpenAI request timed out; provider completion is unknown\".into(),\n+        }\n+    } else {\n+        // Connection failures and other pre-response transport errors: the\n+        // request never reached the provider (or never got a response\n+        // started), so nothing was billed — safe to classify as retryable.\n+        AdapterError::Retryable(RetryableKind::TransientTransport)\n+    }\n+}"},{"kind":"verification","check_id":"tests-workspace-advisory","output":{"content_hash":"sha256:9007f4a5b1430e7280062279f2b7aed48f51bad5629913a2ea483e8f1155b6af","media_type":"text/plain","byte_size":89496,"repository":"/home/trollboy/.local/state/familiar-ai/worktrees/drive-00001788303088789870-0004098830-000000/PRD-60","revision":"sha256:49e9a5c93f21ad24fc7944024c69bccf49e488927d8176f3abb819c523d578c6","storage_ref":"/home/trollboy/.local/share/familiar-ai/review-artifacts/sha256-9007f4a5b1430e7280062279f2b7aed48f51bad5629913a2ea483e8f1155b6af-stdout","truncated":false,"omitted_bytes":0}}],"remediation":"Split the two failure sites: keep `map_transport_error` for `send()` (pre-response) failures, and classify any failure from `response.text()` — the body was already being produced by the provider — as `AdapterError::Ambiguous` with a reason naming the truncated body. Add a fixture that returns a 200 whose body terminates early (e.g. a mismatched content-length or dropped connection) and assert `Ambiguous`, mirroring the existing timeout test.","status":"open","supersedes":null},{"finding_id":"F2-sse-crlf-frames","category":"correctness_defect","severity":"medium","blocking":false,"title":"SSE frame splitting only recognizes LF-LF separators, so CRLF-delimited streams yield zero events","claim":"`parse_sse_events` splits the body on the literal `\"\\n\\n\"`. The SSE specification permits CR LF, LF, or CR line terminators, and intermediaries may normalize to CRLF. A CRLF-delimited body contains no `\"\\n\\n\"` substring, so the entire response becomes one frame whose concatenated `data:` payloads form invalid JSON, producing an empty event list. Every such response then falls through to the no-terminal-event branch and is reported `Ambiguous`, even for a fully successful, fully billed completion. Every test in the change constructs frames with `\\n\\n`, so no fixture exercises the other legal terminator.","evidence":[{"kind":"diff_hunk","path":"crates/familiar-ai-llm/src/openai_api.rs","hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,1367 @@\n+fn parse_sse_events(body: &str) -> Vec<Value> {\n+    let mut events = Vec::new();\n+    for frame in body.split(\"\\n\\n\") {\n+        let mut data = String::new();\n+        for line in frame.lines() {\n+            if let Some(chunk) = line.strip_prefix(\"data:\") {\n+                data.push_str(chunk.trim_start());\n+            }\n+        }\n+        if data.is_empty() || data == \"[DONE]\" {\n+            continue;\n+        }\n+        if let Ok(value) = serde_json::from_str::<Value>(&data) {\n+            events.push(value);\n+        }\n+    }\n+    events\n+}"},{"kind":"verification","check_id":"tests-green-crates","output":{"content_hash":"sha256:571de986e29faf87de308cd77e62715060b04e5e62cfde2746f7f9c8d355b6b8","media_type":"text/plain","byte_size":33731,"repository":"/home/trollboy/.local/state/familiar-ai/worktrees/drive-00001788303088789870-0004098830-000000/PRD-60","revision":"sha256:49e9a5c93f21ad24fc7944024c69bccf49e488927d8176f3abb819c523d578c6","storage_ref":"/home/trollboy/.local/share/familiar-ai/review-artifacts/sha256-571de986e29faf87de308cd77e62715060b04e5e62cfde2746f7f9c8d355b6b8-stdout","truncated":false,"omitted_bytes":0}}],"remediation":"Normalize line endings before splitting (or split on a blank line detected via `lines()` accumulation rather than a fixed `\\n\\n` separator), and add a deterministic fixture whose SSE body uses CRLF terminators asserting the same completed outcome as the LF fixture.","status":"open","supersedes":null},{"finding_id":"F3-structured-output-strict-true","category":"correctness_defect","severity":"medium","blocking":false,"title":"Structured output forces `strict: true` on a caller-supplied schema that may not satisfy the strict subset","claim":"`structured_output_to_format` emits `\"strict\": true` unconditionally around whatever JSON Schema document the caller placed in `StructuredOutputRequest.json_schema`, and silently substitutes `{\"type\":\"object\"}` when that document does not parse. OpenAI's strict structured-output mode accepts only a restricted schema subset (notably requiring `additionalProperties: false` on every object and every declared property listed in `required`); a caller schema that is valid JSON Schema but outside that subset is rejected by the provider with a 400 that this adapter maps to `NonRetryable(InvalidRequest)`. The only coverage is `structured_output_maps_to_json_schema_format`, which asserts the emitted JSON shape and never round-trips a schema through the strict-mode surface, so the failure is invisible to the fixtures.","evidence":[{"kind":"diff_hunk","path":"crates/familiar-ai-llm/src/openai_api.rs","hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,1367 @@\n+fn structured_output_to_format(request: &StructuredOutputRequest) -> Value {\n+    let schema = serde_json::from_str::<Value>(&request.json_schema)\n+        .unwrap_or_else(|_| json!({\"type\": \"object\"}));\n+    json!({\n+        \"type\": \"json_schema\",\n+        \"name\": request.schema_name,\n+        \"schema\": schema,\n+        \"strict\": true,\n+    })\n+}"},{"kind":"verification","check_id":"tests-green-crates","output":{"content_hash":"sha256:571de986e29faf87de308cd77e62715060b04e5e62cfde2746f7f9c8d355b6b8","media_type":"text/plain","byte_size":33731,"repository":"/home/trollboy/.local/state/familiar-ai/worktrees/drive-00001788303088789870-0004098830-000000/PRD-60","revision":"sha256:49e9a5c93f21ad24fc7944024c69bccf49e488927d8176f3abb819c523d578c6","storage_ref":"/home/trollboy/.local/share/familiar-ai/review-artifacts/sha256-571de986e29faf87de308cd77e62715060b04e5e62cfde2746f7f9c8d355b6b8-stdout","truncated":false,"omitted_bytes":0}}],"remediation":"Either derive `strict` from the request (defaulting to non-strict for arbitrary caller schemas), or normalize the schema into the strict subset before setting the flag; and stop silently replacing an unparseable schema with `{\"type\":\"object\"}` — an unparseable structured-output schema should be an explicit `InvalidRequest` at the adapter boundary rather than a silently weakened constraint. Document whichever rule is chosen in `docs/contracts/openai-adapter.md`, which currently states the schema is passed \"exactly as the caller's StructuredOutputRequest supplies\".","status":"open","supersedes":null},{"finding_id":"F4-no-production-wiring","category":"unverifiable_claim","severity":"medium","blocking":false,"title":"No changed file wires `openai-api` into a PRD-057 spec, runtime registry, or credential configuration — the adapter is constructible only from tests","claim":"The change adds the client, the adapter type, a contract document, and tests, but `changed_files` contains no registry, worker-spec, runtime-dispatch, or configuration file. `crates/familiar-ai-agent/src/lib.rs` gains only `pub mod openai;`. Every construction of `OpenAiInferenceAdapter` in the change lives in a test, and the daemon test's own comments state that the shared `persist_run_outcome` helper has no field for the resolved model or provider response id, with the enrichment performed by test-local `AccountingRepository` calls. On the disclosed evidence I cannot confirm the acceptance claims that the adapter is reachable \"behind a PRD-057 spec with runtime openai-api\", that resolved-model identity and provider response identity reach PRD-051 observations in shipped code, or that a credential is resolved on any production path; the passing checks establish only that the new code compiles and its own tests pass.","evidence":[{"kind":"diff_hunk","path":"crates/familiar-ai-agent/src/lib.rs","hunk":"@@ -2,6 +2,7 @@ mod agent;\n mod claude_code;\n mod codex;\n mod isolation;\n+pub mod openai;\n pub mod raw_runtime;\n mod registry;"},{"kind":"verification","check_id":"tests-workspace-advisory","output":{"content_hash":"sha256:9007f4a5b1430e7280062279f2b7aed48f51bad5629913a2ea483e8f1155b6af","media_type":"text/plain","byte_size":89496,"repository":"/home/trollboy/.local/state/familiar-ai/worktrees/drive-00001788303088789870-0004098830-000000/PRD-60","revision":"sha256:49e9a5c93f21ad24fc7944024c69bccf49e488927d8176f3abb819c523d578c6","storage_ref":"/home/trollboy/.local/share/familiar-ai/review-artifacts/sha256-9007f4a5b1430e7280062279f2b7aed48f51bad5629913a2ea483e8f1155b6af-stdout","truncated":false,"omitted_bytes":0}}],"remediation":"Either add the wiring — a worker-spec/runtime registration for `openai-api`, the credential descriptor plumbing that constructs the adapter at the boundary, and the production code path that carries `response_meta` into the accounting row — or state explicitly in the task record which of those are deliberately deferred to a follow-up, so the acceptance criteria are not read as satisfied by test-only construction.","status":"open","supersedes":null},{"finding_id":"F5-tests-assert-framework-not-change","category":"test_gap","severity":"medium","blocking":false,"title":"Accounting, price-schedule and idempotency tests exercise test-local code paths rather than any code introduced by this change","claim":"In `crates/familiar-ai-daemon/tests/openai_adapter.rs`, `resolved_model_binds_a_versioned_dated_price_schedule_to_a_local_estimate` builds the schedule struct, computes `amount_nanousd` with arithmetic written in the test, and INSERTs both the schedule and the `cost_estimates` row with raw SQL; `provider_response_identity_and_resolved_model_enrich_the_ledger` constructs `source_event_hash` and both `UsageObservation` values in the test body. These assert pre-existing `AccountingRepository`/schema behavior, so the acceptance criteria on versioned dated price schedules, exactly-once accounting persistence, and identity enrichment would still pass if the production enrichment and estimation logic were absent — which, per F4, appears to be the case.","evidence":[{"kind":"diff_hunk","path":"crates/familiar-ai-daemon/tests/openai_adapter.rs","hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,534 @@\n+    // Every price-relevant dimension this schedule declares, applied to\n+    // the exact categories this adapter recorded distinctly.\n+    let amount_nanousd = (400 * rate.uncached_input_nanousd_per_million.unwrap()) / 1_000_000\n+        + (100 * rate.cache_read_nanousd_per_million.unwrap()) / 1_000_000\n+        + (40 * rate.output_nanousd_per_million.unwrap()) / 1_000_000\n+        + (15 * rate.reasoning_output_nanousd_per_million.unwrap()) / 1_000_000;"},{"kind":"verification","check_id":"tests-green-crates","output":{"content_hash":"sha256:571de986e29faf87de308cd77e62715060b04e5e62cfde2746f7f9c8d355b6b8","media_type":"text/plain","byte_size":33731,"repository":"/home/trollboy/.local/state/familiar-ai/worktrees/drive-00001788303088789870-0004098830-000000/PRD-60","revision":"sha256:49e9a5c93f21ad24fc7944024c69bccf49e488927d8176f3abb819c523d578c6","storage_ref":"/home/trollboy/.local/share/familiar-ai/review-artifacts/sha256-571de986e29faf87de308cd77e62715060b04e5e62cfde2746f7f9c8d355b6b8-stdout","truncated":false,"omitted_bytes":0}}],"remediation":"Move the estimate computation and the observation/source-event-hash construction into product code invoked by the test, then assert the persisted rows produced by that code. If no such production path is in scope for this task, mark these tests as demonstrations of the existing storage contract rather than as coverage of the PRD-060 accounting criteria.","status":"open","supersedes":null},{"finding_id":"F6-tap-message-discards-diagnostics","category":"maintainability_issue","severity":"low","blocking":false,"title":"`TapMessage` discards the provider's error message for every taxonomy except `Ambiguous`, contrary to its own doc comment","claim":"`tap_message` is documented as attaching human-readable context to an `AdapterError`, but its implementation matches only `AdapterError::Ambiguous` and returns every other variant unchanged. In `map_http_error` the provider `message` is therefore computed and dropped for auth, rate-limit, invalid-request, refused-content and server-error responses — the exact cases where daemon-side diagnostics would matter. In `map_failed_response` no branch can produce `Ambiguous`, so the trait is a no-op there in every path. The abstraction reads as if diagnostics are preserved while none are.","evidence":[{"kind":"diff_hunk","path":"crates/familiar-ai-llm/src/openai_api.rs","hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,1367 @@\n+/// Attaches human-readable context to an [`AdapterError`] without changing\n+/// its taxonomy — the loop only branches on the variant, but daemon-side\n+/// diagnostics benefit from the provider's own message.\n+trait TapMessage {\n+    fn tap_message(self, message: String) -> Self;\n+}\n+\n+impl TapMessage for AdapterError {\n+    fn tap_message(self, message: String) -> Self {\n+        match self {\n+            AdapterError::Ambiguous { .. } => AdapterError::Ambiguous { reason: message },\n+            other => other,\n+        }\n+    }\n+}"},{"kind":"verification","check_id":"lint","output":{"content_hash":"sha256:8afff58348647d955ff574b14ce19b1dbbc0e132debf0876d64f192c247cc794","media_type":"text/plain","byte_size":1268,"repository":"/home/trollboy/.local/state/familiar-ai/worktrees/drive-00001788303088789870-0004098830-000000/PRD-60","revision":"sha256:49e9a5c93f21ad24fc7944024c69bccf49e488927d8176f3abb819c523d578c6","storage_ref":"/home/trollboy/.local/share/familiar-ai/review-artifacts/sha256-8afff58348647d955ff574b14ce19b1dbbc0e132debf0876d64f192c247cc794-stdout","truncated":false,"omitted_bytes":0}}],"remediation":"Either log or otherwise surface the provider message on the non-ambiguous paths (a `tracing` event at the mapping site is enough, given the taxonomy carries no message field), or delete the trait and the now-unused `message` bindings and drop the doc comment's claim.","status":"open","supersedes":null},{"finding_id":"F7-cache-write-field-unverified","category":"unverifiable_claim","severity":"low","blocking":false,"title":"The `input_tokens_details.cache_write_tokens` field is asserted as verified provider behavior from a source the change says was unreachable","claim":"Both the module header and the contract document state as a \"verified deviation\" that, as of 2026-09-01, the Responses API usage object reports `input_tokens_details.cache_write_tokens`, while the same documents state the interactive API reference was not fetchable and that verification rested on SDK type definitions. No disclosed verification artifact corroborates the field's existence — the fixtures assert only that a hand-written payload containing it round-trips. The runtime behavior is safe either way (the field stays `None` when absent, so no category is fabricated), but the normative documentation records a provider fact the package cannot support.","evidence":[{"kind":"diff_hunk","path":"crates/familiar-ai-llm/src/openai_api.rs","hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,1367 @@\n+//! **Verified deviation from the PRD-060 design note (2026-08-30):** the\n+//! design assumed the provider reports no cache-write category. As of\n+//! 2026-09-01 the Responses API usage object *does* report\n+//! `input_tokens_details.cache_write_tokens`. This module maps it into\n+//! [`UsageCategories::cache_write_tokens`] distinctly whenever the provider\n+//! sends it and leaves it `None` only when the provider omits it — no\n+//! category is fabricated either way; the row simply reflects what the\n+//! provider currently reports."},{"kind":"verification","check_id":"tests-green-crates","output":{"content_hash":"sha256:571de986e29faf87de308cd77e62715060b04e5e62cfde2746f7f9c8d355b6b8","media_type":"text/plain","byte_size":33731,"repository":"/home/trollboy/.local/state/familiar-ai/worktrees/drive-00001788303088789870-0004098830-000000/PRD-60","revision":"sha256:49e9a5c93f21ad24fc7944024c69bccf49e488927d8176f3abb819c523d578c6","storage_ref":"/home/trollboy/.local/share/familiar-ai/review-artifacts/sha256-571de986e29faf87de308cd77e62715060b04e5e62cfde2746f7f9c8d355b6b8-stdout","truncated":false,"omitted_bytes":0}}],"remediation":"Soften the wording from \"verified\" to a defensively-parsed optional field (the code already treats it as optional), or cite the exact SDK type and version in the contract document so a later reader can re-verify the claim.","status":"open","supersedes":null}]}
