{"review_id":"00001788306112275771-0004098830-000002-cycle-review-2","reviewed_manifest_hash":"sha256:de0d95ba8fe16a9b57b75654d960d2642370e5ae4c483e23fafc9102cbfa9676","findings":[{"finding_id":"F1-body-read-error-misclassified","category":"correctness_defect","severity":"high","blocking":false,"title":"Body-read failure after status is now classified Ambiguous","claim":"Resolved. `OpenAiResponsesClient::submit` no longer routes the `response.text().await` failure through `map_transport_error`; it maps it directly to `AdapterError::Ambiguous` with an explicit comment that status and headers have already been received so the provider has accepted, executed and billed the request. A dedicated raw-TCP fixture (`truncated_body_after_status_is_ambiguous_never_a_free_retry`) sends valid status/headers and then drops the connection with `Content-Length` unmet, asserting the error surfaces as `Ambiguous` with \"provider completion is unknown\", and the contract document records the same rule.","evidence":[{"kind":"diff_hunk","path":"crates/familiar-ai-llm/src/openai_api.rs","hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,1431 @@\n+        // Unlike `send()` above, status and headers have already been\n+        // received here — the provider has accepted, executed, and billed\n+        // the request. A failure while reading the body is a mid-stream\n+        // cutoff, never a free retry.\n+        let text = response.text().await.map_err(|error| AdapterError::Ambiguous {\n+            reason: format!(\"OpenAI response body could not be read; provider completion is unknown: {error}\"),\n+        })?;"},{"kind":"verification","check_id":"tests-workspace-advisory","output":{"content_hash":"sha256:ec1580e9d2998ccdf0910e1a5ca61431e8fe0957f1223ab652888e8e5cf50d98","media_type":"text/plain","byte_size":89587,"repository":"/home/trollboy/.local/state/familiar-ai/worktrees/drive-00001788303088789870-0004098830-000000/PRD-60","revision":"sha256:7ed3c8d61081a866a0da2cad6825a093691cd4dfc9778de97f1a13c6456bb5f0","storage_ref":"/home/trollboy/.local/share/familiar-ai/review-artifacts/sha256-ec1580e9d2998ccdf0910e1a5ca61431e8fe0957f1223ab652888e8e5cf50d98-stdout","truncated":false,"omitted_bytes":0}}],"remediation":"No further action; the defect is fixed and covered by a deterministic fixture.","status":"resolved","supersedes":null},{"finding_id":"F2-duplicate-tool-call-complete-uncovered","category":"test_gap","severity":"medium","blocking":false,"title":"No fixture replays both terminal function-call events, so duplicate ToolCallComplete is unexercised","claim":"`consume_stream` emits `StreamEvent::ToolCallComplete` for the same `item_id` on both `response.function_call_arguments.done` and `response.output_item.done` (a single match arm covering both event types, with no record of which call ids have already been completed). The real Responses stream sends both events for one function-call item, so a live stream would deliver two `ToolCallComplete` events per `call_id`. Every fixture in this change emits only `response.function_call_arguments.done` and never `response.output_item.done`, so the duplicate-completion path — and whether the PRD-058 collector tolerates it or turns it into a second validated call — is never exercised, despite the acceptance criterion requiring deterministic fixtures covering streaming tool calls.","evidence":[{"kind":"diff_hunk","path":"crates/familiar-ai-llm/src/openai_api.rs","hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,1431 @@\n+                \"response.function_call_arguments.done\" | \"response.output_item.done\" => {\n+                    let item_id =\n+                        event\n+                            .get(\"item_id\")\n+                            .and_then(Value::as_str)\n+                            .unwrap_or_else(|| {\n+                                event\n+                                    .get(\"item\")\n+                                    .and_then(|item| item.get(\"id\"))\n+                                    .and_then(Value::as_str)\n+                                    .unwrap_or(\"\")\n+                            });\n+                    if let Some(call_id) = item_call_ids.get(item_id).cloned() {\n+                        observer.on_event(StreamEvent::ToolCallComplete {\n+                            call_id: call_id.clone(),\n+                        });\n+                    }\n+                }"},{"kind":"diff_hunk","path":"crates/familiar-ai-agent/tests/openai.rs","hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,643 @@\n+                json!({\"type\": \"response.function_call_arguments.delta\", \"item_id\": \"item_1\", \"delta\": \"{\\\"path\\\":\\\"src/lib.rs\\\"}\"}),\n+                json!({\"type\": \"response.function_call_arguments.done\", \"item_id\": \"item_1\"}),\n+                completed(\n+                    \"resp_1\",\n+                    \"gpt-5\",\n+                    json!([{\"type\": \"function_call\", \"id\": \"item_1\", \"call_id\": \"call_1\", \"name\": \"read-file\", \"arguments\": \"{\\\"path\\\":\\\"src/lib.rs\\\"}\"}]),\n+                    usage(20, 0, 5, 0),\n+                ),"},{"kind":"verification","check_id":"tests-green-crates","output":{"content_hash":"sha256:0d0dddb7c0853ce9028f3a79f973ded8679bef602cd7ff271828cceb5e90c38b","media_type":"text/plain","byte_size":33775,"repository":"/home/trollboy/.local/state/familiar-ai/worktrees/drive-00001788303088789870-0004098830-000000/PRD-60","revision":"sha256:7ed3c8d61081a866a0da2cad6825a093691cd4dfc9778de97f1a13c6456bb5f0","storage_ref":"/home/trollboy/.local/share/familiar-ai/review-artifacts/sha256-0d0dddb7c0853ce9028f3a79f973ded8679bef602cd7ff271828cceb5e90c38b-stdout","truncated":false,"omitted_bytes":0}}],"remediation":"Add a fixture that replays the provider's actual terminal sequence for one function-call item — `response.function_call_arguments.done` followed by `response.output_item.done` carrying the same item id — and assert exactly one tool execution and one `ToolCallComplete` per `call_id`. If the loop's collector does not tolerate a repeated completion, track completed item ids in `consume_stream` and emit `ToolCallComplete` only once per call.","status":"open","supersedes":null},{"finding_id":"F3-unbounded-per-attempt-maps","category":"maintainability_issue","severity":"low","blocking":false,"title":"Per-attempt metadata and function-call replay caches grow without bound","claim":"`OpenAiInferenceAdapter::meta` inserts one `OpenAiResponseMeta` per attempt and `OpenAiResponsesClient::call_cache` inserts one `CachedCall` per model-issued `call_id`, with no eviction, no scoping to an execution, and no documented lifetime bound beyond the adapter instance. Both maps are keyed by strings supplied by the provider or the caller, so an adapter reused across a long-running or multi-execution worker accumulates entries indefinitely; the replay cache additionally replays stale calls into every future turn that references an old `call_id`.","evidence":[{"kind":"diff_hunk","path":"crates/familiar-ai-agent/src/openai.rs","hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,130 @@\n+        let (outcome, meta) = self.client.submit(&responses_request, observer).await?;\n+        self.meta\n+            .lock()\n+            .unwrap_or_else(|error| error.into_inner())\n+            .insert(request.attempt_id.0.clone(), meta);\n+        Ok(outcome)"},{"kind":"diff_hunk","path":"crates/familiar-ai-llm/src/openai_api.rs","hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,1431 @@\n+        // Only now that the turn is a confirmed success do the replayed\n+        // function-call items join the durable cache — a failed/ambiguous\n+        // attempt must not poison the next turn's replay with calls the\n+        // model may reissue differently.\n+        let mut cache = self.call_cache.lock().unwrap_or_else(|e| e.into_inner());\n+        cache.extend(new_calls);"},{"kind":"verification","check_id":"lint","output":{"content_hash":"sha256:4b0cce7b4f8941b625a5d741a9b2130991534fb81dec9546e2fb65b15bba9213","media_type":"text/plain","byte_size":1268,"repository":"/home/trollboy/.local/state/familiar-ai/worktrees/drive-00001788303088789870-0004098830-000000/PRD-60","revision":"sha256:7ed3c8d61081a866a0da2cad6825a093691cd4dfc9778de97f1a13c6456bb5f0","storage_ref":"/home/trollboy/.local/share/familiar-ai/review-artifacts/sha256-4b0cce7b4f8941b625a5d741a9b2130991534fb81dec9546e2fb65b15bba9213-stdout","truncated":false,"omitted_bytes":0}}],"remediation":"State and enforce the intended lifetime of both maps: document that an adapter instance is constructed per execution and assert it, or bound the maps (cap size / drop entries once an attempt's metadata has been consumed and once a `call_id` no longer appears in the message history passed to `build_input_items`).","status":"open","supersedes":null}]}
