{"review_id":"00001788308111360583-0004098830-000003-cycle-review-1","reviewed_manifest_hash":"sha256:3a450bf5de7111e2bac0d861d93d590d39c40f8e9a1e9d20828df31ec780fe08","findings":[{"finding_id":"xai-reasoning-tokens-unpriced","category":"correctness_defect","severity":"high","blocking":false,"title":"Reasoning tokens are subtracted from output_tokens but the Grok schedule prices no reasoning rate, so estimates under-count spend","claim":"`map_usage` splits `completion_tokens` into `output_tokens = completion_tokens - reasoning_tokens` and `reasoning_output_tokens = reasoning_tokens`, while the Grok price schedule this change introduces sets `reasoning_output_nanousd_per_million: None` for every model. Reasoning tokens are billed by xAI at the completion rate, so any Grok attempt that reports `completion_tokens_details.reasoning_tokens > 0` yields a local-estimate cost that omits those tokens entirely. Every streamed fixture in the change pins `reasoning_tokens` to 0, so no test exercises the non-zero path where the two decisions interact.","evidence":[{"kind":"file_range","path":"crates/familiar-ai-llm/src/xai_api.rs","range":{"start":295,"end":335}},{"kind":"file_range","path":"crates/familiar-ai-agent/tests/xai.rs","range":{"start":300,"end":355}},{"kind":"verification","check_id":"tests-green-crates","output":{"content_hash":"sha256:d61abc55f325c39544d2dcbe0e96afba0fe728d2b308a3d7398b3194d0724916","media_type":"text/plain","byte_size":33510,"repository":"/home/trollboy/.local/state/familiar-ai/worktrees/drive-00001788303088789870-0004098830-000000/PRD-61","revision":"sha256:2b08903c25cc0c12cc3930ae119724a89781d3619121641c1ecd8324894d2d33","storage_ref":"/home/trollboy/.local/share/familiar-ai/review-artifacts/sha256-d61abc55f325c39544d2dcbe0e96afba0fe728d2b308a3d7398b3194d0724916-stdout","truncated":false,"omitted_bytes":0}}],"remediation":"Either populate `reasoning_output_nanousd_per_million` with the same rate as `output_nanousd_per_million` for every Grok entry (xAI bills reasoning at the completion rate), or stop subtracting reasoning from `output_tokens` and record reasoning purely as an informational sub-count. Add a fixture whose final usage chunk reports non-zero `reasoning_tokens` and assert the resulting estimate covers them.","status":"open","supersedes":null},{"finding_id":"xai-text-tokens-uncached-assumption","category":"unverifiable_claim","severity":"medium","blocking":false,"title":"`uncached_input_tokens` is read from `prompt_tokens_details.text_tokens`, a modality breakdown, on an unverifiable documentation claim","claim":"`map_usage` populates `uncached_input_tokens` from `prompt_tokens_details.text_tokens` and `cache_read_tokens` from `prompt_tokens_details.cached_tokens`, with a comment asserting `text_tokens` is the documented \"uncached\" breakdown. The contract document itself lists `prompt_tokens_details.{text_tokens,cached_tokens,audio_tokens,image_tokens}` — a set whose other members (`audio_tokens`, `image_tokens`) are modality categories, which makes `text_tokens` most plausibly a modality count that also includes cached text tokens rather than a cache-exclusive count. If so, a request with cache hits is counted twice on the input side (once as uncached, once as cache-read). I cannot verify the field's semantics from this package, and no fixture distinguishes the two readings: every streamed usage fixture in the change pins `cached_tokens` to 0, where both interpretations agree.","evidence":[{"kind":"verification","check_id":"tests-green-crates","output":{"content_hash":"sha256:d61abc55f325c39544d2dcbe0e96afba0fe728d2b308a3d7398b3194d0724916","media_type":"text/plain","byte_size":33510,"repository":"/home/trollboy/.local/state/familiar-ai/worktrees/drive-00001788303088789870-0004098830-000000/PRD-61","revision":"sha256:2b08903c25cc0c12cc3930ae119724a89781d3619121641c1ecd8324894d2d33","storage_ref":"/home/trollboy/.local/share/familiar-ai/review-artifacts/sha256-d61abc55f325c39544d2dcbe0e96afba0fe728d2b308a3d7398b3194d0724916-stdout","truncated":false,"omitted_bytes":0}},{"kind":"file_range","path":"crates/familiar-ai-llm/src/xai_api.rs","range":{"start":295,"end":335}}],"remediation":"Record the exact documentation passage that establishes whether `text_tokens` excludes `cached_tokens`. If it does not, derive `uncached_input_tokens` as `text_tokens - cached_tokens` (saturating) or leave it unknown. Add a fixture with `cached_tokens` non-zero and strictly less than `text_tokens` so the two readings produce different assertions.","status":"open","supersedes":null},{"finding_id":"xai-not-reachable-from-production","category":"maintainability_issue","severity":"high","blocking":false,"title":"No production path constructs XaiAdapter or registers the xai provider; the new identity constants have no consumers","claim":"`XaiAdapter` is only ever constructed inside `#[cfg(test)]` modules and the three new test files; nothing in the daemon, registry, or configuration path builds one from an operator's `provider = \"xai\"` / `runtime = \"xai-api\"` worker entry. `GROK_MODEL_FAMILY` and `XAI_CAPABILITY_PROFILE` in `crates/familiar-ai-agent/src/xai.rs` likewise have no non-test reader — the module's own doc comment states the authoritative capability record is expected to live in operator-written configuration, which this change does not read or validate. The only non-test change to `familiar-ai-daemon` is a `wiremock` dev-dependency. As shipped, selecting a Grok worker is not possible through any user-facing surface, so the acceptance criterion that xAI \"is its own ProviderId with runtime xai-api\" holds in tests and prose only.","evidence":[{"kind":"file_range","path":"crates/familiar-ai-agent/src/xai.rs","range":{"start":1,"end":80}},{"kind":"diff_hunk","path":"crates/familiar-ai-daemon/Cargo.toml","hunk":"@@ -57,3 +57,4 @@ predicates = \"3\"\n nix = { version = \"0.29\", features = [\"signal\"] }\n http-body-util = \"0.1\"\n tower = { version = \"0.5\", features = [\"util\"] }\n+wiremock.workspace = true"},{"kind":"verification","check_id":"lint","output":{"content_hash":"sha256:76f579e461a6b6948751eb6c923b1dd979864e73935519abab1662cd8a460f54","media_type":"text/plain","byte_size":1312,"repository":"/home/trollboy/.local/state/familiar-ai/worktrees/drive-00001788303088789870-0004098830-000000/PRD-61","revision":"sha256:2b08903c25cc0c12cc3930ae119724a89781d3619121641c1ecd8324894d2d33","storage_ref":"/home/trollboy/.local/share/familiar-ai/review-artifacts/sha256-76f579e461a6b6948751eb6c923b1dd979864e73935519abab1662cd8a460f54-stdout","truncated":false,"omitted_bytes":0}}],"remediation":"Wire adapter construction into whatever daemon/registry factory maps a configured worker's `runtime` string to an `InferenceAdapter`, resolving `auth_profile` to the `AuthDescriptor` passed into `XaiAdapterConfig`, and add a test that reaches `XaiAdapter` starting from configuration rather than from a hand-built struct. If wiring is deliberately deferred to a later PRD, say so explicitly in the contract's known-deviations section, since the current text reads as though the provider is usable.","status":"open","supersedes":null},{"finding_id":"xai-price-schedule-tautological-test","category":"test_gap","severity":"medium","blocking":false,"title":"Grok pricing is asserted only against literals defined in the same test function, and no schedule ships outside the test","claim":"`grok_price_schedule_matches_official_xai_pricing_in_nanousd` builds a `PriceScheduleConfig` from literals and then asserts those same literals back out of the map. It invokes no production code, compares against no committed schedule, and would keep passing if every rate in it were wrong. `cost_in_usd_ticks_conversion_is_documented_and_exact` is likewise arithmetic on two local literals with no adapter involvement. No price schedule for Grok is added anywhere outside this test and a fenced example in the contract document, so the acceptance criterion that estimates record a dated Grok schedule is not exercised end to end.","evidence":[{"kind":"file_range","path":"crates/familiar-ai-agent/tests/xai.rs","range":{"start":300,"end":368}},{"kind":"verification","check_id":"tests-green-crates","output":{"content_hash":"sha256:d61abc55f325c39544d2dcbe0e96afba0fe728d2b308a3d7398b3194d0724916","media_type":"text/plain","byte_size":33510,"repository":"/home/trollboy/.local/state/familiar-ai/worktrees/drive-00001788303088789870-0004098830-000000/PRD-61","revision":"sha256:2b08903c25cc0c12cc3930ae119724a89781d3619121641c1ecd8324894d2d33","storage_ref":"/home/trollboy/.local/share/familiar-ai/review-artifacts/sha256-d61abc55f325c39544d2dcbe0e96afba0fe728d2b308a3d7398b3194d0724916-stdout","truncated":false,"omitted_bytes":0}}],"remediation":"Commit the Grok schedule as real configuration (or a checked-in fixture the estimate path loads) and have the test parse that artifact and drive the actual estimate function with a known usage tuple, asserting the resulting cost. Delete or rewrite the two literal-only assertions, whose names promise verification they do not perform.","status":"open","supersedes":null},{"finding_id":"xai-auth-test-cannot-observe-its-claim","category":"test_gap","severity":"medium","blocking":false,"title":"The \"no request ever sent\" auth test cannot distinguish a suppressed request from a request that reached the mock server","claim":"`auth_failure_fails_closed_with_no_request_ever_sent_credentials` mounts no `Mock` and comments that any request \"would be an unexpected-request panic from wiremock\". `MockServer` responds to an unmatched request with HTTP 404 and does not panic or fail the test unless an expectation is registered. A 404 maps through `map_status_error` to `NonRetryable(InvalidRequest)`, which surfaces as the very same `StopReason::ProviderFailure { taxonomy: NonRetryable }` the test asserts — so the assertion holds whether or not the credential check short-circuited before the network call, and the property named in the test's own name goes unverified.","evidence":[{"kind":"file_range","path":"crates/familiar-ai-agent/tests/xai.rs","range":{"start":255,"end":300}},{"kind":"verification","check_id":"tests-green-crates","output":{"content_hash":"sha256:d61abc55f325c39544d2dcbe0e96afba0fe728d2b308a3d7398b3194d0724916","media_type":"text/plain","byte_size":33510,"repository":"/home/trollboy/.local/state/familiar-ai/worktrees/drive-00001788303088789870-0004098830-000000/PRD-61","revision":"sha256:2b08903c25cc0c12cc3930ae119724a89781d3619121641c1ecd8324894d2d33","storage_ref":"/home/trollboy/.local/share/familiar-ai/review-artifacts/sha256-d61abc55f325c39544d2dcbe0e96afba0fe728d2b308a3d7398b3194d0724916-stdout","truncated":false,"omitted_bytes":0}}],"remediation":"Mount a catch-all mock with `.expect(0)` and call `server.verify().await`, or assert `server.received_requests().await` is empty, so the test actually observes that no HTTP request left the adapter. Correct the comment about wiremock's unmatched-request behavior.","status":"open","supersedes":null},{"finding_id":"xai-cancel-does-not-abort","category":"correctness_defect","severity":"medium","blocking":false,"title":"`cancel` records an attempt id but never aborts the in-flight stream, and no fixture covers cancellation mid-stream","claim":"`XaiAdapter::cancel` pushes the `AttemptId` onto a `Mutex<Vec<AttemptId>>` and returns; the streaming read loop in `submit` never consults that list. A cancelled attempt therefore keeps reading chunks and keeps the provider generating (and billing) until the request-level timeout or natural end of stream. The only cancellation coverage in the change is `cancel_is_recorded_for_diagnostics_only`, which calls `cancel` on an adapter that has no request in flight and asserts the id was stored — the acceptance criterion naming cancellation among the required deterministic fixtures is not met. The `cancelled` vector also grows without bound for a long-lived adapter.","evidence":[{"kind":"file_range","path":"crates/familiar-ai-llm/src/xai_api.rs","range":{"start":540,"end":575}},{"kind":"verification","check_id":"tests-green-crates","output":{"content_hash":"sha256:d61abc55f325c39544d2dcbe0e96afba0fe728d2b308a3d7398b3194d0724916","media_type":"text/plain","byte_size":33510,"repository":"/home/trollboy/.local/state/familiar-ai/worktrees/drive-00001788303088789870-0004098830-000000/PRD-61","revision":"sha256:2b08903c25cc0c12cc3930ae119724a89781d3619121641c1ecd8324894d2d33","storage_ref":"/home/trollboy/.local/share/familiar-ai/review-artifacts/sha256-d61abc55f325c39544d2dcbe0e96afba0fe728d2b308a3d7398b3194d0724916-stdout","truncated":false,"omitted_bytes":0}}],"remediation":"Have the chunk loop check the cancelled set (or hold a per-attempt abort handle / `CancellationToken`) between reads and return an `Ambiguous` outcome when the current attempt has been cancelled, then add a fixture that cancels a slow in-flight stream and asserts the request terminates early with ambiguous usage. If aborting is intentionally out of scope, document `cancel` as advisory in the contract instead of implying cancellation coverage.","status":"open","supersedes":null},{"finding_id":"xai-test-env-var-mutation","category":"maintainability_issue","severity":"low","blocking":false,"title":"Tests mutate process environment variables while sibling tests read them concurrently","claim":"`adapter_for`, `xai_adapter`, and the two fail-closed tests call `std::env::set_var` / `std::env::remove_var` at test-body scope. Cargo runs the tests within each binary on multiple threads, so these writes race against `std::env::var` calls made by concurrently running tests in the same binary — a data race that `set_var` is documented as unsound for, and a latent source of flakes that the current green run does not rule out. It also makes the fixtures order-dependent in a way that is invisible at the call site.","evidence":[{"kind":"file_range","path":"crates/familiar-ai-agent/tests/xai.rs","range":{"start":93,"end":102}},{"kind":"file_range","path":"crates/familiar-ai-llm/src/xai_api.rs","range":{"start":585,"end":600}},{"kind":"verification","check_id":"tests-workspace-advisory","output":{"content_hash":"sha256:a27de7e27b604f3adaa498540301ed8fe3af80c06c4f15fb4d90798c288a971f","media_type":"text/plain","byte_size":88537,"repository":"/home/trollboy/.local/state/familiar-ai/worktrees/drive-00001788303088789870-0004098830-000000/PRD-61","revision":"sha256:2b08903c25cc0c12cc3930ae119724a89781d3619121641c1ecd8324894d2d33","storage_ref":"/home/trollboy/.local/share/familiar-ai/review-artifacts/sha256-a27de7e27b604f3adaa498540301ed8fe3af80c06c4f15fb4d90798c288a971f-stdout","truncated":false,"omitted_bytes":0}}],"remediation":"Make the credential source injectable for tests — e.g. accept a resolver closure or an in-process descriptor variant alongside `AuthDescriptor::Env` — so no test needs to mutate the process environment; failing that, serialize the environment-touching tests behind a shared mutex or a single-threaded harness.","status":"open","supersedes":null}]}
