## Findings

**1. Runtime-string → adapter dispatch (subprocess/CLI adapters only, `CodingAgent`)**

`crates/familiar-ai-agent/src/registry.rs` — `AdapterFactories` (trait object registry keyed by runtime id):
- `AdapterFactory` trait: lines 59-62
- `AdapterFactories::register`/`build` (keyed on `worker.runtime_id`): lines 71-89
- Built-in registration point: lines 123-132 (`factories.register(Box::new(CodexFactory{id:"codex"}))`, `"ollama"`, `ClaudeCodeFactory` as `"claude-code"`)

**Important correction to the premise:** this registry builds `Box<dyn CodingAgent>` (subprocess CLI agents), not `Box<dyn InferenceAdapter>` (raw-API). There is **no equivalent factory/registry for raw-API `InferenceAdapter`s in production code**. Confirmed: `grep "impl InferenceAdapter for"` finds only `crates/familiar-ai-llm/src/attempt.rs:289` (`FakeInferenceAdapter`, test-only) and `crates/familiar-ai-llm/src/xai_api.rs:354` (`XaiAdapter`, this PRD's work). No `OpenAiAdapter`/`AnthropicAdapter` raw-API type exists anywhere in this workspace — `docs/contracts/xai-adapter.md:38-39` explicitly disclaims depending on a "PRD-060 OpenAI adapter" that isn't implemented.

**2. `auth_profile` → `AuthDescriptor` resolution**

- Field declared: `crates/familiar-ai-core/src/config/mod.rs:75` — `pub auth_profiles: BTreeMap<String, AuthDescriptor>`.
- Only consumer today is **existence validation**, not resolution: `mod.rs:458-460` checks `self.auth_profiles.contains_key(profile)` when loading `worker_registry.workers`.
- No code path actually does `config.auth_profiles.get(&worker.auth_profile)` to hand an `AuthDescriptor` into an adapter config — that wiring doesn't exist yet. Daemon's `run.rs:1223` only stores `configured_worker.auth_profile.as_deref()` as a string into `worker_specs` (metadata), it never resolves/dereferences it.
- `RegistryWorkerConfig::runtime_id()`: `crates/familiar-ai-core/src/config/registry_workers.rs:309`.

**3. Trait-object registry for `InferenceAdapter`**

None exists. `AdapterFactories` (finding 1) is `CodingAgent`-only. The raw-API loop core (`crates/familiar-ai-agent/src/raw_runtime.rs`, `run_loop` at line 836) and its daemon wiring (`crates/familiar-ai-daemon/src/agent_runtime.rs`) take an already-constructed `&dyn InferenceAdapter` as an argument — nothing in `run.rs` or `agent_runtime.rs` currently builds one from `RegistryWorkerConfig.runtime`/`.auth_profile` in production.

**4. Best existing config-driven construction test to model an xAI test after**

Since no OpenAI/Anthropic precedent exists, the closest and most authoritative pattern is this PRD's own three test layers (already written):
- `crates/familiar-ai-llm/src/xai_api.rs` (`#[cfg(test)]`, e.g. `runtime_id_is_xai_api_never_openai` at line 958) — builds `XaiAdapter::new(XaiAdapterConfig::new(AuthDescriptor::Env(...)))` directly against `wiremock`.
- `crates/familiar-ai-agent/tests/xai.rs` — round-trips a hand-built `XaiAdapter` through unmodified `raw_runtime::run_loop`.
- `crates/familiar-ai-daemon/tests/xai_adapter.rs:1-45` — same construction, plumbed through `SqliteToolJournal`/`persist_run_outcome`.

All three construct `XaiAdapterConfig` by hand-building `AuthDescriptor::Env("...")`, not by loading it from a parsed `[auth_profiles.*]` config table — because, per finding 2, that resolution step doesn't exist in production yet either.
